  "validity_note": "Laliberte (2009) aqueous-electrolyte correlation for CaCl2-water. Tabulated for 2-34 wt% over 0-80 degC. Saturation at 0 degC is about 37 wt% CaCl2, so the 34 wt% ceiling leaves margin below saturation across the whole table; calcium chloride freezing points fall steeply with strength, so every tabulated point is liquid. The correlation's fitted density data for CaCl2 begins at 15 degC; rows below that are a short extension toward 0 degC (its viscosity data extends to 0 degC) and should be treated as indicative at the cold end. Concentrations are anhydrous CaCl2; commercial flake and liquid grades are specified on an as-sold basis that includes water of hydration. Values are for preliminary design; verify against vendor data for critical service.",
